In article <1992Dec22.230413.22738@uicc.com>, putsch@uicc.com (Jeff Putsch) writes:
>I have used MH/MIME with DecWindows dxmail, DEC's xmh-like interface
>to MH, 

Actually, dxmail and xmh have common roots.

>My questions are:
>
>1 - What does the -wait option do?

This was added as a 'bugfix'. To understand why, kill sendmail on your system.
Then, send a mail message using xmh. You get no indication of an error,
but no message gets sent. '-wait' makes mh send wait until it's able to
connect to sendmail before returning control.
[Note: I didn't do this work, and may have the details wrong.. but this is
 approximately the instance that the change was intended to fix.]

>2 - How does one get dxmail (in DecWindows MOTIF) to stop using it?

You can't. (short of editing the binary.) 

>3 - Does anyone know where DEC documents their 'enhancements' to MH?

For '-mts' and '-note', in the manpages.  See below. '-wait' appears to be
a quick fix for a dxmail-specific bug. Command-line mh users would never need
this -- since they'll see the eventual error messages.

>4 - Along with Q3, does anyone know of other options/enhancement to MH
>    that DEC made I might like to know about? For example, what are
>    -mts and -note (see send -help output below)?

'-mts' and '-note' are used for DEC's X.400 mail product.

Now, about your *real* problem - I'd suspect it'd be easy to add a dummy 
'-wait' to the MIME-capable version that ignores it.
