When using the "ARC" item of the xfig (v2.1) drawing program in certain
orientations (including 12,3,6 o'clock [see below]) the arc drawn on the
screen is badly misdrawn.  This occurs with the default line thickness
(thicker is ok), and the default zoom level (larger zoom is ok).
This occurs only on "HX" equipped DECstations (of all the kinds we have).
They are running Ultrix 4.2a.

This would appear to me to be either a bug in Xws or the HX card itself,
but I am wondering if any one else has seen this with something other
than xfig (or conversly, has seen xfig do this on some other system).

Thanks,
John
