  Our primary db application utilizes a DEC 5000/240 as an INGRES server
  (it is dedicated to run an INGRES 6.4 server to front ends on other DEC-
  systems via INGRES/NET).  

  Usage has grown and, as a result, the 5000/240 needs to be replaced.  Our
  need is for a system with at least twice the cpu throughput in terms of 
  single-stream performance; somewhat better i/o, but that is not a bottleneck
  currently; complete INGRES/NET interoperability with DEC and SUN-based 
  INGRES front ends; complete rsh and nfs interoperability with DEC and SUN
  systems.

  We have nowhere to go with DEC (the R4000-based upgrade has been substantial-
  ly delayed and it will be at least a year before INGRES is available on 
  any ALPHA-based systems) so we are looking at other vendors.  Any input,
  mailed directly to me, will be appreciated.


