I've created a new mailing list for the managers of DEC Alpha AXP systems
running OSF/1.  The list is modelled after the DECstation-managers list
(which I also run) and the sun-managers list run by Phil LeFabvre.

This list is intended to provide quick turnaround, so there's a policy
describing exactly what is and isn't allowed.  You'll receive a copy of this
policy when you subscribe, but in a nutshell, only questions and summaries
of responses can be sent to the list.  There is *no* discussion permitted.

To subscribe, send a message to majordomo@sws10.ctd.ornl.gov with the
following command in the body, not the "Subject":

	subscribe alpha-osf-managers

If you'd like to set up an alias at your site for redistributing the list,
you can subscribe it by adding it to the command as follows:

	subscribe alpha-osf-managers alpha-osf-managers@foo.bar

You can also get a copy of the policy statement by sending the command:

	info alpha-osf-managers

to majordomo@sws10.ctd.ornl.gov.

