Eugene,

  I'm afraid that the product literature may have confused you. It is true 
that both the DEC3000/400 and the DEC3000/500 have two separate SCSI-2
channels. However, in both cases one of the NCR53C94 chips is dedicated to
the internal storage. On the DEC3000/500 the internal storage can be up to
6 devices (of which two can be removable media). On the DEC3000/400 the 
internal storage can be up to 3 devices (of which one can be removable media).

  Both of the SCSI-2 interfaces on either machine are DMA based. And I also
believe that CAM SCSI on OSF/1 does support the 7LUN (Logical Unit Numbers)
for each SCSI ID (provided that you have a SCSI controller at that ID that is
capable of using it.

  However, please understand that while the documentation is correct that there
are two entirely separate SCSI-2 channels on each of these workstations, only
one of them goes to the outside.

I hope that helps.

