>Tony Konashenok   avk@hafnium.cchem.berkeley.edu   (510)843-5632 (home)
>University of California, Berkeley                 (510)642-5831 (office)
> 
>Strauss research group, Latimer Hall, UC Berkeley, Berkeley CA 94720, U.S.A.


Two things you can do:

1) Before you do the backup, do:
	$ reply/enable=(central,tapes, ...)   ! see HELP REPLY /ENABLE
This will make your current terminal an operator terminal, and you will then
be able to REPLY to the message from backup.  You will get the message with
a number associated with it, and you will reply with:
	$ reply/to=## YES
so if it is the first message, you would use $ reply/to=1 YES (see HELP REPLY)

2) Use the /NOASSIST qualifier with backup.
	$ backup/noassist/ima/init/log mua0:backup1.sav/sav dua0:

Good luck,
-Shawn

