You might want to look at the (relatively) new LK421 keyboard.  These
are designed for people who like traditional Unix and X-windows.

First of all, the keyboard is only 13.25 inches wide (instead of 19").
There is no separate keypad, although all of the keypad keys are
available as "extend"ed keys from the main keyboard.

The escape key is in the right place (next to "1"), there's no
caps lock key (instead, CTRL is nice and wide), there are two keys
with ~ and ` on them (so that you can choose which placement you want),
and a few other changes have been made (i.e., no </> key between "shift"
and "Z").

You might still need to fiddle with the keymap to get ESC on the right
key.  But the keyboard layout is much better (and the price is the
same as our standard keyboard).

It's not for everyone, but I already have three!

-Jeff

P.S.: Also, if you're like me and you map shift-ESC to "~", you
might have trouble with the mwm window manager unless you change
your .mwmrc to disable the mapping between shift-ESC and f_wmenu.


