Andy,
 
This is a common hazard. It can occur in a variety of cases where 
a account file has been corrupted. The solution is to perform a 
conversational boot (BOOT/R5=1). This will permit you to either 
boot with an alternate account file OR redirect the STARTUP file 
to OPA0, which will provide you with a way to get control of the 
system after the startup file has completed.
 
If I can be of further assistance, please feel free to contact me 
