In article <cozzi.24@convex.rad.nd.edu>, cozzi@convex.rad.nd.edu (Marc D. Cozzi) writes:
>
> I have a need for fairly large file systems and files.
> file size > 4Gbytes
> file systems > 8Gbytes
>
> Does DEC offer disk stripping with Alpha/OSF ?
> If not when if ever will it be available?

OSF/1 on Alpha AXP systems will use 64 bit integers for off_t, allowing
very large files and file systems.  Using LVM on OSF/1 you can take parts
of disks and build large file systems.  This isn't really striping because
the chunks are too large, but it will get you virtual devices of the
required capacity.

If you do end up needing Striping, please let me know.  I'm the person
currently maintaining ULTRIX Striping and will likely have to do it for
OSF if there is need.
