We have a DECstatsion 5000/240 that acts as a server for 6 DEC 3100's.
Since the 5000/240 has the most memory of all our machines (60 Mb +
300 Mb swap) users like to run large jobs on it.  If a user runs a
program that uses about 80% or more of the core memory, the 5000/240
will crash, or hang until it's reset and rebooted.  The error logs on
the 5000/240 don't report anything unusual prior to the crash, and the
system reboots without a problem.  The same programs run on our 3100's
work fine -- no crashes.

Has anyone seen behavior like this, or know what else I can look for
to narrow down the source of problem.

