Richard,

  You don't mention which operating system you are looking to support? I would
gather it's OSF/1 since you're migrating from a DS5000/200? I have seen the
PMAZ-AB in a DEC3000/400 under OSF/1 and believe it is supported (I am trying
to get an official check on the supportment statement). I'm not sure why the
catalog is layed out in that fashion. The PMAZ-AB (TURBOchannel SCSI Adapter)
is a PIO (Programmed I/O) based option. The base SCSI port on the DEC3000/400
(or the DEC3000/500 for that matter) is DMA (Direct Memory Access) based. So,
you may want to consider which ports you hang which devices on (the base SCSI
port on the DS5000/200 is also PIO only).

