The real issue is around the availability of features in the OS that you
rely on, as well as layered products and third party software that you
also rely on.  

From an OS standpoint, OpenVMS AXP today is  a stable OS, from the standpoint
of what's in there.  HOwever, things like Journaling, Volume Shadowing, 
Clustering, and much of the Transaction processing environment isn't there yet.
This is why your sales person is pushing back and suggesting an Alpha-ready
VAX system today.  All of the software you need to run your cricital 
operation is available today.

However, your request of 12/93 makes things a little more interesting.  VMS
will release another version before mid calendar year that includes some things
