I have an ethernet question that I can not get a handle on.  How/When do
you have too many collisions on the ether?  I look after about a dozen
networks, some will have 1Hr util. rates over 35%, 1sec peeks
as hi as 93% (but more likely around the high 70s).  I am seeing one
hour collision rates of over 5% and packet frags in the same ball park.
Some of these nets have over 200 devices on them (maybe way over) and
also may have a dozen or two 10base2 nets connected to them by DEMPERs
(Repeaters).  I am wondering about using a bridge to isolate the 10base2
(DEChub 90s) mostly based on the thought that I will only be seeing one
device (the bridge) vs all the 10base2 devices + repeater frags.

Any comment, advice, war stories, etc. welcome.

