Dan,
 
APPC is part of SNA (It stands for "Logical Unit 6.2"). In rough 
terms, LU 6.2 supports peer-to-peer communications (SNA has its 
history in Host-Terminal communications, unlike DECnet). Until 
fairly recently, SNA required a piece of large iron in the middle 
of the network for intelligence.
 
Offhand, I do not see why one would be considering LU 6.2 
communications in a pure DEC shop. While SNA does support some 
features that DECnet does not support, most of these are rather 
obscure. DECnet supports full task-to-task applications 
communications and has full peer-to-peer support.
 
I hope that the above information is helpful. If I can be of 
further assistance, please feel free to drop me an Email or give 
me a call.
 
