Hi!

I'm trying to set up a DECnet link over asynchronous modem connection
with dynamic switching, between to VAX machines running VMS V5.5

I followed the directions in the Networking Manual, but I have the
following problem:

The circuit (TT-0-2) comes up for a few seconds, then goes into the ON
-STARTING state. After a few seconds more I get a "line synchronisation
lost" message on the console, and the modem disconnects. 

The terminal ports at both ends are set up with /MODEM, /EIGHT and 
/DISCONNECT as suggested by the manual. Does this mean that the ports 
on the VAXes _have_ to support full modem control (RTS/CTS) in order for
this to work? In that case, what do I do with my VAXstation 3100 which
doesn't have any ports with full modem control? The manual says that I
should check whether both machines are set up as endnodes or as
routers. In my case the calling machine is an endnode while the
answering machine is an area router. Is this a problem, or should it
work? Should both machines be set up with the same area number? I feel
tha manual is a bit unclear about this. One more thing: Should the
terminal ports on the VAXes be set up with the _exact_ speed of the
modem connection, or is it OK to let the modems handle any differences
in speed through flow control (XON/XOFF)?

Please reply via e-mail. Thanks!

