Gunnar,
 
As a frequent user and manager for Dial-up Asynch DECnet connections, I 
can testify that they certainly work. Some notes about dial-up 
connections. First, make sure that the passwords are set 
correctly for the node on both sides of the link. Dialup nodes 
MUST use link-level passwords. Often, a password problem on one 
end or the other will show up as the symptoms you describe. 
 
The question of speed should not be a problem on the machines. 
First, the dial-in port will automatically set its speed using 
autobaud during the dialin process. If your modems are going to 
negotiate speed, flow control itself should not be a problem, so 
long as the modems have internal buffering. Xon-Xoff cannot be 
used because DDCMP (the protocol used for asynch DECnet 
connections) is a binary protocol. Instead, there are limits on 
the size and quantity of buffers that can be outstanding at a 
time. 
 
I hope that the above information is helpful. If I have been 
unclear, or if I can be of further assistance, please feel free 
to contact me via Email.
 
